---
title: Well-shaped document
---

The negative half of the document-shape pin. Everything here is the *correct* form of a
defect `skim-shape.tmd` trips, so this file must report zero `TAL-SHAPE-*` diagnostics. A
rule that started firing on ordinary structure would fail here rather than sail through a
green suite.

## Well-shaped document

The leading heading restates the title, which is the ordinary landing-page idiom and is
exempt from `TAL-SHAPE-ECHO` on purpose: four of the fourteen corpus projects open this
way, including both dogfooded books.

## A grouping parent

### A real subsection

A heading followed by *deeper* headings is a grouping parent. It has content in the
document tree, so demanding an intro paragraph under it would be a style opinion rather
than a defect, and `TAL-SHAPE-HOLLOW` leaves it alone.

## A section whose body is not prose

- a list item
- another list item

A section can be carried by a list, a table, a figure or a code cell instead of a
paragraph. Reading "has content" off the rendered blocks is what keeps these clean; an
earlier draft read the `skim` projection, which only sees the first `<p>`, and flagged
11.8% of the corpus.

```python
print("a code cell is content too")
```

